    {
      "id": "r9a7mfp059p452bf",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 48,
      "y": 708,
      "width": 644,
      "height": 134,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 631866099,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 475874655,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730000000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "WHY AN INSTANCE IS REQUIRED TO CONTRIBUTE/UPDATE\n\nBlockVersion.define_source / build_source are BlockVersion.Source messages:\n{ instance, commit_sha }. That's the ONLY mechanism the contribute flow uses to\nsay \"pull these commits\". An Instance is the thing that owns a git branch\n(created by InstallBlock). Without an installed instance, there is no branch to\npoint Source.instance at \u2014 so no commit_sha can be resolved server-side.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 72,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "WHY AN INSTANCE IS REQUIRED TO CONTRIBUTE/UPDATE\n\nBlockVersion.define_source / build_source are BlockVersion.Source messages:\n{ instance, commit_sha }. That's the ONLY mechanism the contribute flow uses to\nsay \"pull these commits\". An Instance is the thing that owns a git branch\n(created by InstallBlock). Without an installed instance, there is no branch to\npoint Source.instance at \u2014 so no commit_sha can be resolved server-side.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "zptx497w19vw3rtq",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 870,
      "width": 660,
      "height": 190,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#f1f3f5",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 495076678,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 259106531,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730000000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "muh8lmn4r7sgmsox",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 48,
      "y": 878,
      "width": 644,
      "height": 174,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 385347786,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 649114719,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730000000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "IS THIS REMOVABLE? \u2014 client convention, not a hard proto rule\n\nCreateBlockVersionRequest carries a full BlockVersion, which ALSO has a\ncontributed_content field (BlockVersion.Content: build/infra/proto files) \u2014\nthe exact same shape BootstrapBlock uses for the FIRST version.\n\nNothing in the .proto forces version UPDATES to go through instance+commit_sha.\nBut neither alis-hub-v3 nor the VS Code extension (the reference client) wires\ncontributed_content into version updates \u2014 only into initial Bootstrap.\nSo: real design constraint of the production flow, in principle relaxable,\nbut doing so would diverge from how the reference client behaves.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 114,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "IS THIS REMOVABLE? \u2014 client convention, not a hard proto rule\n\nCreateBlockVersionRequest carries a full BlockVersion, which ALSO has a\ncontributed_content field (BlockVersion.Content: build/infra/proto files) \u2014\nthe exact same shape BootstrapBlock uses for the FIRST version.\n\nNothing in the .proto forces version UPDATES to go through instance+commit_sha.\nBut neither alis-hub-v3 nor the VS Code extension (the reference client) wires\ncontributed_content into version updates \u2014 only into initial Bootstrap.\nSo: real design constraint of the production flow, in principle relaxable,\nbut doing so would diverge from how the reference client behaves.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "a8ircd9si5gas442",
